            <ArticleTitle>Simultaneous trial of deep brain and motor cortex stimulation in chronic intractable neuropathic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>218-26</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1159/000362933</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND/OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Both motor cortex stimulation (MCS) and deep brain stimulation (DBS) of the ventralis caudalis (Vc) thalamus have been shown to be effective in chronic neuropathic pain, and the modulation of thalamic and thalamocortical activity is regarded as a possible mechanism. Although Vc DBS and MCS have a common analgesic mechanism, the application of MCS and DBS is still considered empirical, and there is no consensus on which method is better.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We performed a simultaneous trial of thalamic Vc DBS and MCS in 9 patients with chronic neuropathic pain and investigated the results of the stimulation trial and long-term pain relief.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Of the 9 patients initially implanted with both DBS and MCS electrodes, 8 (89%) had a successful trial; 6 of these 8 patients (75%) responded to MCS, and the remaining 2 responded to Vc DBS. During the long-term follow-up, the mean numeric rating scale score decreased significantly (p &lt; 0.05). The percentages of pain relief in the chronic MCS group and the chronic DBS group were 37.9 ± 16.5 and 37.5%, respectively, and there was no statistically significant difference (p = 0.157).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Considering the initial success rate and the less invasive nature of epidural MCS compared with DBS, we think that MCS would be a more reasonable initial means of treatment for chronic intractable neuropathic pain.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2014 S. Karger AG, Basel.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
